<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">poisons</ansi>

A vial of poison coats one bladed weapon (slashing, cleaving, or stabbing).
Poison is a way to prepare a company: a coated blade that wounds a foe may
leave a poison in the wound, and the poison works on that foe for a few
combat rounds.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The coating</ansi>

  One vial is one dose for one blade. A dual wielder needs two.
  A coating lasts <ansi fg="yellow">10 real minutes</ansi> or <ansi fg="yellow">8 blows that wound</ansi>, whichever ends first.
  Its time keeps running while you travel or log out.
  A blow that misses, is dodged, parried, blocked, or does no damage uses
  nothing. Each blow that does wound uses one hit and has a
  <ansi fg="yellow">40%</ansi> chance to leave the poison (20% against a resistant foe, none
  against an immune one, such as the dead and things built, not born).
  A critical hit does not raise the chance.
  A blade holds one coating at a time. Clear the old one before adding another.
  Sharpening and coatings work together.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The poisons</ansi> (sold in markets)

  <ansi fg="command">bitterleaf</ansi>   1 damage a round for 3 rounds. Cheap; sold on the road too.
  <ansi fg="command">leechbane</ansi>    The foe's healing is cut by a quarter for 3 rounds. Use it
               against healers.
  <ansi fg="command">leadroot</ansi>     The foe's physical blows do 15% less damage for 2 rounds.
               Use it on a dangerous striker.
  <ansi fg="command">mirethorn</ansi>    The foe's dodge chance is 10 points lower for 2 rounds.

A foe carries one poison at a time. Another coated hit does not stack or
refresh it, however many of your company carry coated blades. Mixing
poisons across the company helps when members fight different foes.
Poisons count combat rounds and end with the fight. A cleric's cleansing
(<ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>) and <ansi fg="command">curepoison</ansi> take them off. Healing and
<ansi fg="command">heal wounds</ansi> do not.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">coat</ansi> [poison] [<ansi fg="command">self</ansi>|member] [<ansi fg="command">main</ansi>|<ansi fg="command">off</ansi>]
  Put one dose on one blade (default: your main hand), not in a fight and
  not while travelling or resting. <ansi fg="command">coat bitterleaf</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">coat leadroot Corvin off</ansi>.

  <ansi fg="command">coat status</ansi>
  Show the vials you carry and every blade's coating, with minutes and
  hits left.

  <ansi fg="command">coat clear</ansi> [<ansi fg="command">self</ansi>|member] [<ansi fg="command">main</ansi>|<ansi fg="command">off</ansi>]
  Wipe a coating off. The dose is lost.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">At camp</ansi>

Set up the whole company at once with a preparation list. It spends nothing
until you apply it, and applies all of it or none of it:

  <ansi fg="command">camp poison</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">camp poison assign</ansi> [member|<ansi fg="command">self</ansi>] [<ansi fg="command">main</ansi>|<ansi fg="command">off</ansi>] [poison]
  <ansi fg="command">camp poison unassign</ansi> [member|<ansi fg="command">self</ansi>] [<ansi fg="command">main</ansi>|<ansi fg="command">off</ansi>]
  <ansi fg="command">camp poison preview</ansi>   exact doses needed, and anything blocking
  <ansi fg="command">camp poison apply</ansi>     spend the doses and coat every assigned blade

Vials come from your company's supplies (cargo first, then packs). Blades
already coated with the assigned poison are skipped without a dose. If any
blade is blocked, or the vials run short, nothing is spent and every
problem is listed.

Inventories, <ansi fg="command">conditions</ansi>, and the gear window show a blade's coating, and the
fight lines name the poison on the blow that left it, such as
<ansi fg="command">(3 damage, bitterleaf)</ansi>. See also <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>, and
<ansi fg="command">help sharpen</ansi>.
